    "body": "I think there is a subtle distinction in some of these cases. At least in my mind.\r\n\r\nA \"line break\" is a typographical feature, about lines breaking into two.\r\n\r\nA \"newline\" is a CR/LF/CRLF code point sequence.\r\n\r\nI'm not sure this is a distinction worth keeping, but it does seem like this pull request obviates it, and we should be sure we're OK with that.",
